<h3 style="color:#0055A5;border-bottom:2px solid #0055A5;padding-bottom:4px">Consequences of Expiry</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Immediate sales ban</b> in all 30 EEA countries</li>
<li><b>Customs seizure</b> of products at EU borders</li>
<li><b>Recall obligation</b> for products already placed on the market</li>
<li><b>Market surveillance authorities</b> may impose fines (up to €500,000 per violation)</li>
<li><b>Distributor liability</b> — EU distributors will refuse to stock un-certified products</li>
<li><b>Loss of existing contracts</b> with EU customers requiring CE compliance</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color:#0055A5;border-bottom:2px solid #0055A5;padding-bottom:4px">Renewal Process</h3>
<p>To renew your CE certification, we require:</p>

<p><b>Step 1 — Submit Technical Documentation:</b></p>
<p>Upload the following documents through our <b>Certification Client Portal</b>:</p>
<ol>
<li><b>Updated Risk Assessment</b> — per EN 62368-1:2020 Annex B</li>
<li><b>Technical Construction File (TCF)</b> — updated for latest product revisions (v1.9.5)</li>
<li><b>Schematics & PCB layouts</b> — for all three models</li>
<li><b>Bill of Materials (BOM)</b> — with safety-critical components highlighted</li>
<li><b>Test Reports</b> — updated EMC & Safety test reports (from accredited lab)</li>
<li><b>User Manual</b> — in all EU languages currently supported</li>
<li><b>Declaration of Conformity (DoC)</b> — draft for our review</li>
<li><b>Factory Production Control (FPC)</b> — updated quality management documentation</li>
</ol>

